32	/**
33	 * The claims on a sheet: listed newest first, added to a person and edited one at a time. A claim
34	 * added with no date takes the entry date while one is set, else the sheet's today (an edit with none, the sheet's today). Its due-by is fixed when it is added: the terms-th business day
35	 * after its date (skipping weekends and the sheet's holidays then), with its person's own terms, else the terms in force on that date of its person's grade then (else the
36	 * sheet's terms in force on it); it does not
37	 * move when its date or the terms change later. A claim is added as DRAFT and moves through its statuses
38	 * as {@link ClaimStatus} allows; a change it does not allow is refused. Opening a claim gives it
39	 * the sheet's next number (or, while the sheet numbers by period, the next within its period), which it
40	 * keeps when voided and is never given again. Only a DRAFT claim
41	 * can be edited; an OPEN one is changed by voiding it and adding a new one. Settling it
42	 * fixes its due at its figure (the due bound by a statement, else its person's grade rate of the
43	 * moment on the claim's date) with its late charge of the moment frozen in; with no figure it
44	 * stays live. A steward can re-settle a SETTLED claim at the figure it would have today as an open claim
45	 * bound by no statement, or void it within 7 days of its settlement: its frozen figure leaves every total
46	 * and it keeps its number. The user who opened a claim cannot settle it, and a clerk cannot settle one whose
47	 * due is above the sheet's clerk limit (a steward can). A claim with no proofs whose due is above the proof threshold
48	 * in force on its date cannot be settled or approved by anyone, and one with an empty note whose due is above the
49	 * note threshold in force on its date cannot be opened. No claim whose due-by falls inside a closed period can
50	 * be added, edited (to or from such a date), opened, settled, re-settled or voided. No claim can be added
51	 * or edited to a date after its person's retirement date. A claim with a negative amount is a
52	 * correction: it must name, by number, a SETTLED claim of the same person; only a correction may name one.
53	 * A steward can re-date an OPEN or PENDING claim ({@link #redate}). A DRAFT claim can be deleted, and
54	 * restored to DRAFT on the same sheet's today ({@link #delete}, {@link #restore}).
55	 */
